        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Chapters"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. [Structured Data Output (JSON)](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/01_structured_data_output__json__.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. [HTML Content Ingestion](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/02_html_content_ingestion_.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. [PDF Resource Discovery](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/03_pdf_resource_discovery_.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. [Automated File Downloading](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/04_automated_file_downloading_.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. [Dynamic File Organization](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/05_dynamic_file_organization_.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. [Slug Generation Utility](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/06_slug_generation_utility_.md)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Generated by [AI Codebase Knowledge Builder](https://github.com/The-Pocket/Tutorial-Codebase-Knowledge)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Welcome to the `sandbox` project! This tutorial will guide you through how different parts of this project work together. Let's start with how we store the information we find."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Imagine you're a librarian, and your job is to go through a large collection of web pages to find all the links to PDF documents. For each PDF, you want to note down its title, its web address (URL), and the category it belongs to (like \"Math Homework\" or \"History Notes\")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Once you have this list for a webpage, how do you save it so that:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. You can easily read it later?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. A computer program (perhaps one that downloads all these PDFs) can understand it without mistakes?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. You could potentially upload this list to a website or a database?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is where **Structured Data Output** comes in, and in our project, we use a popular format called **JSON**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What is JSON, Anyway?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "JSON stands for **J**ava**S**cript **O**bject **N**otation. That might sound a bit technical, but the idea is simple! Think of JSON as a way to write down information in a very organized list, much like a librarian creating a detailed catalog card for each book."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A JSON \"catalog\" can contain:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-47",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Objects**: These are like individual catalog cards. An object holds details about one specific item, using `key: value` pairs. For example, a PDF \"object\" might look like this:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```json"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"title\": \"Introduction to Science\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"url\": \"<http://example.com/intro_science.pdf>\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"category\": \"Science Reports\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here, `\"title\"`, `\"url\"`, and `\"category\"` are the \"keys\" (like labels on a form), and `\"Introduction to Science\"`, `\"<http://example.com/intro_science.pdf>\"`, and `\"Science Reports\"` are their corresponding \"values\"."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-57",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Arrays**: These are ordered lists of items. If you have many PDFs, you can put their \"objects\" into an array. An array is marked by square brackets `[]`, and items are separated by commas."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```json"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "["
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"title\": \"PDF One\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"url\": \"link1.pdf\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"category\": \"General\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "},"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"title\": \"PDF Two\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"url\": \"link2.pdf\","
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"category\": \"Specifics\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-72",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-73",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This array holds two PDF objects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "JSON is great because it's easy for humans to read (with a little practice!) and very easy for computers to create and understand. This makes it perfect for sharing data between different programs or systems."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Why `sandbox` Uses JSON"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In our `sandbox` project, the first major task is to look inside HTML files, find all the links to PDF documents, and extract important details about them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-77",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Once we have this list of PDF details, we need to store it. JSON is our chosen format because:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **It's Standardized**: Many tools and programming languages can work with JSON."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **It's Readable**: We can open a `.json` file and see the data clearly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **It's Flexible**: It can represent the simple or complex data structures we need. The way we structure our JSON (our \"schema\") is influenced by how we might want to use this data later, as discussed in `notes/schema_breakdown.md`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The `sandbox` script will create one `.json` file for each HTML file it processes. This JSON file will contain a list (an array) of all the PDF resources found in that HTML."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How `sandbox` Creates JSON: A Peek into the Process"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's say our script processes an HTML file named `course-materials.html`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Finding Information**: The script first reads `course-materials.html`. It then looks for specific patterns to find links to PDFs, their titles, and the categories they belong to. (We'll learn more about this in [HTML Content Ingestion](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/02_html_content_ingestion_.md) and [PDF Resource Discovery](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/03_pdf_resource_discovery_.md))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Collecting the Data**: As it finds each PDF, it creates a small JavaScript object with `title`, `url`, and `category` properties. All these objects are collected into a list (an array in JavaScript)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Imagine our script found two PDFs in `course-materials.html`. In JavaScript, the collected data might look like this:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```jsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "// This is what the 'resources' array might look like in the script"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const resources = ["
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{ title: \"Chapter 1 Notes\", url: \"chap1.pdf\", category: \"Course Notes\" },"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "{ title: \"Syllabus\", url: \"syllabus.pdf\", category: \"General Info\" }"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "];"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This `resources` array holds the information for all PDFs found in one HTML file."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Converting to JSON and Saving**: The script then needs to save this `resources` array into a file."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- It first determines a filename for the JSON file, often based on the original HTML filename. For example, `course-materials.html` might lead to `course-materials.json`. The script uses a helper to create these neat filenames, which you'll learn about in [Slug Generation Utility](https://www.notion.so/turtlelabs/06_slug_generation_utility_.md)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-97",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Then, it converts the `resources` array into a JSON formatted string."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Finally, it writes this string to the `.json` file."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here's a simplified snippet showing how JavaScript data is turned into a JSON string and prepared for saving:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-100",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```jsx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-101",
